      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "ὡς οἶσθα καὶ σύ, μικρῷ τάχιον εἰπὼν ὡς πᾶσα ὑπόθεσις ἀνασκευάζεται καὶ κατασκευάζεται",
          "english_quote": "as you yourself know from what I said a little earlier: every thesis can be refuted and established",
          "issue": "The explicit local subject σύ supplies the natural referent of εἰπών: the addressee said this earlier. The draft instead supplies the present speaker as the earlier speaker and introduces “from what I said.” Its note acknowledges the second-person reading but gives no grammatical or contextual reason for departing from the explicit local subject; merely stating that εἰπών is taken as first person does not substantiate that attribution.",
          "suggested_revision": "Use the source-transparent attachment: “as you yourself know, having said a little earlier that every thesis can be refuted and established.” Any retained first-person proposal would need a substantive source-based explanation, not merely an assertion of the chosen referent.",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἀποδείξει γὰρ μιᾷ τῇ ἀπ’ ἀρχῆς καὶ ἀκριβεῖ ἐξετάσει τῇ πανταχόθεν τὰ ὅλα ὀρθῷ εἴληπται λογισμῷ.",
          "english_quote": "for through one proof—the exact examination made at the outset and from every side—the whole has been rightly grasped by sound reasoning.",
          "issue": "The ordinary construction coordinates a single proof from the outset with a precise examination from every side. The draft instead identifies the examination with the proof and moves “at the outset” into the description of the examination. An explanatory reading of καί can be considered, but the note neither preserves the materially different coordinated reading nor explains why identification is preferred. The current disclosure is therefore insufficient under the supplied ambiguity policy.",
          "suggested_revision": "A source-transparent revision is: “for by a single proof from the outset and by a precise examination from every side, everything has been grasped with sound reasoning.” If an explanatory rendering of καί is proposed instead, preserve the coordinated alternative in a note and explain the contextual basis for that choice.",
          "severity": "major"
        }
      ]
